    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d288">

                <pb facs="0376" n="274" sameAs="frus:frus1933v03/pg274"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/6176: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China (Johnson) to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-04-14T13:00:00+08:00">April 14, 1933—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received April 14—5:05 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>330. Yoshizawa<anchor n="90" xml:id="d288-f1"/> visited Peiping. I am informed
                    that he was not able to see any Chinese of importance here or in the South. I
                    believe purpose of his visit was to inform himself of current Chinese reactions
                    to Japanese occupation of Jehol and activities along Wall. He left impressed
                    with fact that for the time being no Chinese are prepared to commit themselves
                    to negotiations direct or indirect. I believe that he expects a change of
                    government in May or at latest in July and that Seiyukai<anchor n="91"
                        xml:id="d288-f2"/> will succeed present government and that he will be
                    Minister of Foreign Affairs. He was accompanied by Count Iwaki of the House of
                    Peers and Mr. Hashimoto of the Diet.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Tokyo.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d288-f1" n="90" xml:id="d288-f1-content">
                <p>Kenkichi Yoshizawa, member Japanese House of Peers.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d288-f2" n="91" xml:id="d288-f2-content">
                <p>Seiyukai Party.</p>
            </note>
